# Flow CLI flag surface

`pebbles flow` renders the issue dependency graph. This fixture locks the
flag surface of loan 70c871cf: `--format` (text default), `--output`
(required for non-text formats), `--show-done`, and `--goal`. The dot
backend is live (loan ea4b09f2); json is still not implemented (loan
e7dd87ca) and fails with a clear error.

The text layout renders each dependency layer as a column under one
"Layer N:" header row. Each issue is one cell: an indicator glyph
("→" gates other work, "⚠" is blocked by a non-Done dependency, "✓"
is ready), the minimal ID prefix, and the title (truncated at
30 chars). Disconnected components are separated by an empty line;
standalone issues form a trailing list without a glyph.

Fixture store: des-22222222 (Design auth flow) is required_for
uc-33333333 (Implement login); bug-11111111 (Login bug) is done and
standalone.

## Default: text to stdout, completed issues hidden

```console
$ pebbles flow
═══ Project Flow ═══

Layer 0:                  Layer 1:
→ 222 Design auth flow  ⚠ 333 Implement login

```

## --show-done includes completed issues

The done bug appears in the standalone section.

```console
$ pebbles flow --show-done
═══ Project Flow ═══

Layer 0:                  Layer 1:
→ 222 Design auth flow  ⚠ 333 Implement login

Standalone issues (1 total):
  111 Login bug

```

## --goal resolves its ID today; highlighting lands in loan e4937f0b

The flag parses and validates the goal ID. Highlighting the critical chain
to the goal is the separate loan e4937f0b.

```console
$ pebbles flow --goal 22222222
═══ Project Flow ═══

Layer 0:                  Layer 1:
→ 222 Design auth flow  ⚠ 333 Implement login

```

## Non-text formats require --output

```console
$ pebbles flow --format svg
? 1
Error: --output <path> is required for the 'svg' format (only text writes to stdout)

```

## json backend is not implemented yet (dot is live)

```console
$ pebbles flow --format json -o flow.json
? 1
Error: json output is not implemented yet; only 'text' and 'svg' are available

```
